msgid "stage401-large.573"
msgstr "... my brother Karl, for example, has spent half his life looking for the world's largest diamond ..."

msgid "stage401-large.574"
msgstr "... and Gunther, my other brother, an archaeologist, he's tenaciously seeking the sacred chamber of Amesis-Huni ..."

msgid "stage401-large.575"
msgstr "Like I told you my friend, we Heckers are very stubborn, if nothing else!"

msgid "stage401-large.576"
msgstr "Then why haven't you finished the job yet?"

msgid "stage401-large.577"
msgstr "Because all this time I've never managed to lower this damn drawbridge."

msgid "stage401-large.578"
msgstr "I've explored the area around and I know these walls like the palm of my hand but I haven't found a way in ..."

msgid "stage401-large.579"
msgstr "I don't know how the hell to go in there!"

msgid "stage401-large.580"
msgstr "Well, I must leave you now."

msgid "stage401-large.581"
msgstr "Take care and remember ..."

msgid "stage401-large.582"
msgstr "... Keep an eye out for those damn vampires. Anything can fall on you from above!"

msgid "stage401-large.583"
msgstr "Tell me about it."

msgid "stage401-large.584"
msgstr "Ah, you see, it's a very interesting story ..."

msgid "stage401-large.585"
msgstr "... It was built in Samarkand by the famous Arab alchemist Kabir Alfajor more than nine hundred years ago ..."

msgid "stage401-large.586"
msgstr "... His goal was to capture in a container the first light of dawn, that supposedly contained unbelievable magical properties."

msgid "stage401-large.587"
msgstr "In those days, the creation of the formula for the Philosopher's Stone, with which one could make gold, was every alchemist's dream ..."

msgid "stage401-large.588"
msgstr "... and Kabir after studying ancient forbidden Persian rituals for decades he managed to give the powers of the Stone to a medallion."

msgid "stage401-large.589"
msgstr "For years this miraculous invention was lost until it reappeared in the hands of the Templars, who used it as a relic in their ancient holy rites ..."

msgid "stage401-large.590"
msgstr "... However, the fate of the medallion was lost in a terrible shipwreck and was found years later by a little Viking boy named Valdemar ..."

msgid "stage401-large.591"
msgstr "or was it Valdegorm?"

msgid "stage401-large.592"
msgstr "So, how does the medallion work?"

msgid "stage401-large.593"
msgstr "It's simple. You just open it in front of the person or object you want to bathe in its sunlight."

msgid "stage401-large.594"
msgstr "Can I take a look?"

msgid "stage401-large.595"
msgstr "No way."

msgid "stage401-large.596"
msgstr "It has cost me way too much time and effort to track it down, for me to part with it, even for a second."

msgid "stage401-large.597"
msgstr "Why don't you rest for a while, my friend? You look exhausted. Give me the medallion and I'll finish off Dracula for you."

msgid "stage401-large.598"
msgstr "I appreciate it, but it's my duty. I will not rest until I have personally destroyed this despicable nest of evil."

msgid "stage401-large.599"
msgstr "It's also personal."

msgid "stage401-large.600"
msgstr "Well, I think we should drop this subject."

msgid "stage401-large.601"
msgstr "Whatever."

msgid "stage401-large.602"
msgstr "Good ..."

msgid "stage401-large.603"
msgstr "... Nice..."

msgid "stage401-large.604"
msgstr "... Okay, that's enough."

msgid "stage401-large.605"
msgstr "But wait, the best has yet to come ..."

msgid "stage401-large.606"
msgstr "... when Valdemar was captured ten years later in the Silk Road heading to the Orient by ..."

msgid "stage401-large.607"
msgstr "Excuse me, but I really wanted to ask you something else."

msgid "stage401-large.608"
msgstr "Okay, ask whatever you want."

