msgstr " stairs"

msgid "stage209-small.2"
msgstr " altar"

msgid "stage209-small.3"
msgstr " entrance"

msgid "stage209-large.500"
msgstr "I did it! ..."

msgid "stage209-large.501"
msgstr "... This is definitely the altar of Karnak!"

msgid "stage209-large.502"
msgstr "The stairs lead up to the altar."

msgid "stage209-large.503"
msgstr "It seems like marble inlaid with gold ..."

msgid "stage209-large.504"
msgstr "... they certainly spared no expense!"

msgid "stage209-large.505"
msgstr "It communicates with the sarcophagi chamber."

msgid "stage209-large.506"
msgstr "First I have to get something personal of the Princess."

msgid "stage209-large.507"
msgstr "First I have to get pollen from a flower of the Nile"

msgid "stage209-large.508"
msgstr "First I have to get something personal of the Princess and pollen from a flower of the Nile."

msgid "stage209-large.509"
msgstr "Well, I have everything I need ..."

msgid "stage209-large.510"
msgstr "... a hair of the Princess ..."

msgid "stage209-large.511"
msgstr "... pollen from a flower of the Nile ..."

msgid "stage209-large.512"
msgstr "... let's see how it goes ..."

msgid "stage209-large.513"
msgstr "KARNAK! ..."

msgid "stage209-large.514"
msgstr "... karuba ses akos ba! ..."

msgid "stage209-large.515"
msgstr "... tupisfer karros sala! ..."

msgid "stage209-large.516"
msgstr "... astreser sis a dof pres!"

msgid "stage209-large.517"
msgstr "Good! It seems to be working ...!"

msgid "stage209-large.518"
msgstr "Well, if it has worked, I know a certain someone who will be very grateful ..."

msgid "stage209-large.519"
msgstr "I think I'd better wait for the right moment to use the parchment and cast the spell."

msgid "stage210-small.1"
msgstr " stone door"

msgid "stage210-small.2"
msgstr " outside of the pyramid"

msgid "stage210-small.3"
msgstr " bookshelf"

msgid "stage210-small.4"
msgstr " armchair"

msgid "stage210-small.5"
msgstr " Staff of Ra"

msgid "stage210-large.500"
msgstr "It's full of strange hieroglyphics."

msgid "stage210-large.501"
msgstr "It can be opened only with the Staff of Ra."

msgid "stage210-large.502"
msgstr "All these books are about Egypt ..."

msgid "stage210-large.503"
msgstr "... Except maybe this one here: “Get out of my life and back to your grave” ..."

msgid "stage210-large.504"
msgstr "... It must be really good!"

msgid "stage210-large.505"
msgstr "It looks really comfortable."

msgid "stage210-large.506"
msgstr "I wouldn't mind a rest ..."

msgid "stage210-large.507"
msgstr "... but I think I'd better leave it for later."

msgid "stage210-large.508"
msgstr "My grandfather, Amenophis, gave me this advice ..."

msgid "stage210-large.509"
msgstr "... If you want to protect your treasure from outisiders ..."

msgid "stage210-large.510"
msgstr "... You'd best put everything in a magically sealed room ..."

msgid "stage210-large.511"
msgstr "... That only my Staff can open it."

msgid "stage210-large.512"
msgstr "Good morning, my friend!"

msgid "stage210-large.513"
msgstr "Who are you? What do you want? ..."

msgid "stage210-large.514"
msgstr "... I can't find my beloved wife anywhere. Know anything about it?"

msgid "stage210-large.515"
msgstr "... well, yeah... I mean, NO."

msgid "stage210-large.516"
msgstr "No. Absolutely not. The truth is I have no idea."

msgid "stage210-large.517"
msgstr "Then please leave me. I can't waste any more time. I have to find her."

msgid "stage210-large.518"
msgstr "Okay, okay. I'm leaving. Good luck!"

msgid "stage210-large.519"
msgstr "Hello, my friend!"

msgid "stage210-large.520"
msgstr "I'm going to LIVE again!"

msgid "stage210-large.521"
msgstr "I'm free! I just can't believe it!"

msgid "stage210-large.522"
msgstr "At last I can go to Las Vegas and have the time of my life like I so deserve ..."

msgid "stage210-large.523"
msgstr "... after having to endure... well, all that I have endured all these years."

msgid "stage210-large.524"
msgstr "That's LIFE!"

msgid "stage210-large.525"
msgstr "It always feels so nice to help your fellow man!"

msgid "stage210-large.526"
msgstr "Good morning, what can I do for you?"

msgid "stage210-large.527"
msgstr "Hi, I'm Ron Ashman, a reporter for The Quill and I'd like a few minutes of your time.\t"

msgid "stage210-large.528"
msgstr "I'm listening, Mr. Ashman."

msgid "stage210-large.529"
msgstr "Good morning."

msgid "stage210-large.530"
msgstr "Good morning, Mr. Ashman."

msgid "stage210-large.531"
msgstr "Congratulations on your award for Best Dramatic Role."

msgid "stage210-large.532"
msgstr "Thank you very much."

msgid "stage210-large.533"
msgstr "How is your wife, Princess Amesis-Huni?"

msgid "stage210-large.534"
msgstr "Don't even mention her name to me ..."

msgid "stage210-large.535"
msgstr "... She'll bury me alive if she could."

msgid "stage210-large.536"
msgstr "How was the party in Hannover's castle?"

msgid "stage210-large.537"
msgstr "Well, the truth is I was a little nervous and didn't have a great time."

msgid "stage210-large.538"
msgstr "At every party we go, my wife just has to make a sorry spectacle of herself ..."

msgid "stage210-large.539"
msgstr "... She gets herself really drunk and then starts to flirt with anybody she meets."

msgid "stage210-large.540"
msgstr "Tell me more about this maze ..."

msgid "stage210-large.541"
msgstr "The Maze of Horus was built centuries ago by the wisest architects of the Empire and no one has gotten out alive from there."

msgid "stage210-large.542"
msgstr "It joins the two chambers of the Sacred Seal and also communicates with the Sphinx and the altar of Karnak."

msgid "stage210-large.543"
msgstr "And what about this terrible curse?"

msgid "stage210-large.544"
msgstr "No one knows what it really is ..."

msgid "stage210-large.545"
msgstr "... because no one, who's ever reached the altar of Karnak, lived to tell about it."

msgid "stage210-large.546"
msgstr "Could you show me your Award?"

msgid "stage210-large.547"
msgstr "With pleasure. Right here."

msgid "stage210-large.548"
msgstr "I won't take up any more of your time. Have a nice day."

msgid "stage210-large.549"
msgstr "It's been a pleasure."

msgid "stage210-large.550"
msgstr "Anybody???"

msgid "stage210-large.551"
msgstr "Anybody. Although she picks them younger and younger every time ..."

msgid "stage210-large.552"
msgstr "Pathetic!"

msgid "stage210-large.553"
msgstr "But isn't she the love of your life?"

msgid "stage210-large.554"
msgstr "She was Mr. Ashman, She was ..."

msgid "stage210-large.555"
msgstr "... But since I resurrected her with an old Egyptian spell, she's only interested in luxuries and earthly pleasures."

msgid "stage210-large.556"
msgstr "She has squandered away most of my fortune and truth be told no one can stand her for more than five minutes."

msgid "stage210-large.557"
msgstr "I wish I could go back in time and just leave her in the Afterlife. I should never have resurrected  her.\t"

msgid "stage210-large.558"
msgstr "I understand she can be a bit unpleasant ..."

msgid "stage210-large.559"
msgstr "Unpleasant???"

msgid "stage210-large.560"
msgstr "She's like a rat in a pyramid, only with more perfume and jewelry."

msgid "stage210-large.561"
msgstr "Then why don't you send her back to the Afterlife?"

msgid "stage210-large.562"
msgstr "I am forbidden by the Gods ..."

msgid "stage210-large.563"
msgstr "... In order to bring her back to life I made a pact that prevents me from ever sending her back ..."

msgid "stage210-large.564"
msgstr "... It's the price I have to pay, to spend with her the rest of my life."

msgid "stage210-large.565"
msgstr "If you can find someone to get rid of her, I would be eternally grateful to you."

msgid "stage210-large.566"
msgstr "What would it take to get rid of her?"

msgid "stage210-large.567"
msgstr "The way to return someone, who's been resurrected, back to the Afterlife is quite simple ..."

msgid "stage210-large.568"
msgstr "... You just need to sprinkle pollen of the flower of the Nile on a quite personal item belonging to the resurrected one and then recite aloud the incantation."

msgid "stage210-large.569"
msgstr "Get yourself together... You're an immortal."

msgid "stage210-large.570"
msgstr "I know... and that's what makes my situation a lot worse!"

msgid "stage210-large.571"
msgstr "What exactly is this incantation?"

msgid "stage210-large.572"
msgstr "The parchment with the spell to return someone, who's been resurrected, back to the Afterlife is very easy to get ..."

msgid "stage210-large.573"
msgstr "... Actually it can be found at almost any market stall around here."

msgid "stage210-large.574"
msgstr "It sounds very easy. Are you sure that's all I have to do?"

msgid "stage210-large.575"
msgstr "Ah, the tricky part comes next ..."

msgid "stage210-large.576"
msgstr "... You see, for the spell to work it has to be read aloud at the altar of Karnak ..."

msgid "stage210-large.577"
msgstr "... and to get there there's no other choice but to go through the terrible Maze of Horus."

msgid "stage210-large.578"
msgstr "My grandfather, Amenophis, gave me this advice ..."

msgid "stage210-large.579"
msgstr "... If you want to protect your treasure from outisiders ..."

msgid "stage210-large.580"
msgstr "... You'd best put everything in a magically sealed room ..."

msgid "stage210-large.581"
msgstr "... That only your Staff can open it."

