msgstr " Jack The Ripper"

msgid "stage105-small.6"
msgstr " briefcase"

msgid "stage105-small.7"
msgstr " Charlie"

msgid "stage105-large.500"
msgstr "It leads to the lobby."

msgid "stage105-large.501"
msgstr "He looks like a nice guy."

msgid "stage105-large.502"
msgstr "I believe Charlie will go far."

msgid "stage105-large.503"
msgstr "I can't take it without the receipt for the wardrobe."

msgid "stage105-large.504"
msgstr "I wonder why it's not hanging with the others."

msgid "stage105-large.505"
msgstr "It seems to cover something behind it."

msgid "stage105-large.506"
msgstr "Well, let's see ..."

msgid "stage105-large.507"
msgstr "Here you go, friend."

msgid "stage105-large.508"
msgstr "Thank you."

msgid "stage105-large.509"
msgstr "Better not to disturb a guy with that kind of reputation ..."

msgid "stage105-large.510"
msgstr "He's Jack The Ripper."

msgid "stage105-large.511"
msgstr "He's sleeping it off. Looks like he had too much to drink last night."

msgid "stage105-large.512"
msgstr "I don't think he'll miss it in his condition."

msgid "stage105-large.513"
msgstr "It's one of those briefcases that the doctors always carry."

msgid "stage105-large.514"
msgstr "Hi, I'm Ron Ashman of The Quill."

msgid "stage105-large.515"
msgstr "Hello, I'm Charlie Bog, in charge of the wardrobe and future movie star."

msgid "stage105-large.516"
msgstr "For a moment I thought you were the reincarnation of Robert Feynman, the old actor ..."

msgid "stage105-large.517"
msgstr "... you look just like him in his heyday."

msgid "stage105-large.518"
msgstr "Hi, Charlie."

msgid "stage105-large.519"
msgstr "Hello, Ron."

msgid "stage105-large.520"
msgstr "Why do you want to be a movie star?"

msgid "stage105-large.521"
msgstr "Since I was a kid I've always dreamed of reaching the top."

msgid "stage105-large.522"
msgstr "I'm sure I can be the best horror film star in history."

msgid "stage105-large.523"
msgstr "Have you seen around a colleague of mine, Sue Bergman?"

msgid "stage105-large.524"
msgstr "I may have, the truth is that the name sounds familiar ..."

msgid "stage105-large.525"
msgstr "... but a lot of people pass through here and to be honest I only notice the famous ones."

msgid "stage105-large.526"
msgstr "You know, the actors, the directors, the producers ..."

msgid "stage105-large.527"
msgstr "Did you notice anything unusual during the party?"

msgid "stage105-large.528"
msgstr "Anything unusual? ..."

msgid "stage105-large.529"
msgstr "... Parties in Hollywood are always unusual. Other than that nothing."

msgid "stage105-large.530"
msgstr "Tell me about the Awards ceremony."

msgid "stage105-large.531"
msgstr "The Academy Of Motion Pictures Arts and Sciences grants Awards to the best of the best every year."

msgid "stage105-large.532"
msgstr "And everybody who's anybody gathers just to see the winners ..."

msgid "stage105-large.533"
msgstr "... but to be honest, I think the main reason they come is to laugh at the nominees who don't get the Award."

msgid "stage105-large.534"
msgstr "This year the Werewolf grabed, or should I say pawed, the most coveted one, the Actor of the Year Award and was the big winner of the night ..."

msgid "stage105-large.535"
msgstr "... He was also about to win the Best Dramatic Role, but in the end it was wrapped around the Mummy. You should have seen how the Werewolf howled."

msgid "stage105-large.536"
msgstr "Only the Dracula wasn't really satisfied with the outcome of the ceremony. He managed to sunk his teeth only on the Honorary Award For Lifetime Achievement."

msgid "stage105-large.537"
msgstr "... He didn't even thank the Academy."

msgid "stage105-large.538"
msgstr "He refuses to believe that his career is finished, unlike most people."

msgid "stage105-large.539"
msgstr "I assume you know everything about movie stars, right?"

msgid "stage105-large.540"
msgstr "Well, yes! Ask me whatever you want."

msgid "stage105-large.541"
msgstr "Later, Charlie."

msgid "stage105-large.542"
msgstr "Okay, bye."

msgid "stage105-large.543"
msgstr "I hate to tell you this, Charlie, but you don't look scary enough to become a famous monster."

msgid "stage105-large.544"
msgstr "Well, I can do something that no one else can."

msgid "stage105-large.545"
msgstr "What can you tell me about Count Dracula?"

msgid "stage105-large.546"
msgstr "Dracula was the greatest ..."

msgid "stage105-large.547"
msgstr "... No one overshadowed him and he always managed to sink his teeth on the best roles."

msgid "stage105-large.548"
msgstr "But nowadays he just sucks. The producers are bleeding money and in the end he's not profitable for them ..."

msgid "stage105-large.549"
msgstr "... He's now become an old bat himself, basking on his glory days, and a pale shadow of what he was."

msgid "stage105-large.550"
msgstr "He lives in a castle in the Carpathians, in the heart of Transylvania, and he doesn't go out much ..."

msgid "stage105-large.551"
msgstr "... And that's one of the reasons why he ceased to be popular."

msgid "stage105-large.552"
msgstr "What do you know about Frankenstein?"

msgid "stage105-large.553"
msgstr "Frankenstein doesn't make many films per year. He's very selective about the parts he chooses for himself and participates only in high quality productions."

msgid "stage105-large.554"
msgstr "He's very popular with the public, although he's not really the life or the heart of Hollywood ..."

msgid "stage105-large.555"
msgstr "... He usually never attends a party, with very few exceptions."

msgid "stage105-large.556"
msgstr "In fact, only a few people know that he's an intellectual. He prefers to work on his experiments and scientific treatises in his country house at the foot of the Swiss Alps."

msgid "stage105-large.557"
msgstr "What can you tell me about the Werewolf?"

msgid "stage105-large.558"
msgstr "He broke all box office records with his latest film and his sex appeal and raw animal magnetism make all the women swoon over him."

msgid "stage105-large.559"
msgstr "No one knows exactly where he lives, but his lair is rumored to be in what was once the largest diamond mine in the world, somewhere in Australia."

msgid "stage105-large.560"
msgstr "It's true he's been lucky, but I guess you could say that he's just seized his opportunities ...  "

msgid "stage105-large.561"
msgstr "... I hope to be as great as him someday."

msgid "stage105-large.562"
msgstr "What about the Mummy?"

msgid "stage105-large.563"
msgstr "The Mummy is a very eccentric actor."

msgid "stage105-large.564"
msgstr "He has a certain resemblance to Frankenstein, but Sakhem, as is his real name, makes many more films every year ..."

msgid "stage105-large.565"
msgstr "... The gossips say that he does so in order to maintain the over the top lifestyle of his wife Princess Amesis-Huni."

msgid "stage105-large.566"
msgstr "He lives in a magnificent pyramid in Egypt, on the banks of the Nile, but every time there's a party in Hollywood, his wife drags him there."

msgid "stage105-large.567"
msgstr "Tell me about the other famous actors."

msgid "stage105-large.568"
msgstr "There're many less known monsters that have made their way on the big screen and made a name for themselves ..."

msgid "stage105-large.569"
msgstr "... like Junior or the Swamp Thing."

msgid "stage105-large.570"
msgstr "But there are also others like the Golem or Fu-Manchu ..."

msgid "stage105-large.571"
msgstr "... who only make utter garbage films."

msgid "stage105-large.572"
msgstr "What about the actresses?"

msgid "stage105-large.573"
msgstr "There haven't been many important roles for women in this industry yet ..."

msgid "stage105-large.574"
msgstr "... Although there are exceptions, like the Countess Bartoli, the beautiful panther-woman, or Stella the Murder Doll, but I think she has turned to hardcore porn lately."

msgid "stage105-large.575"
msgstr "In any case, most of the actresses in horror movies tend to be the victims ..."

msgid "stage105-large.576"
msgstr "... the “Scream Queens” as I like to call them."

msgid "stage105-large.577"
msgstr "I have enough information, thanks Charlie."

msgid "stage105-large.578"
msgstr "You're welcome, Ron. And remember me. Someday I'll be up there in the charts."

msgid "stage105-large.579"
msgstr "Absolutely!!! I'm sure you'll go far."

msgid "stage105-large.580"
msgstr "Thank you, I practice every day in front of a mirror, you know ..."

msgid "stage105-large.581"
msgstr "... One day soon my chance will come, I'm sure of it."

